    "created_at": "2019-07-26T05:03:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-26T05:04:12Z",
    "body": "I guess it depends on how we go about it. I had assumed that we'd compute the duration of the last command outside of starship as part of the `starship init` script, so that it can be passed in as a flag.\r\n\r\n- **fish**: we can pass in `$CMD_DURATION` as a flag\r\n- **zsh**: we use `preexec()` and `precmd()` to check a timer and subtract, then pass that as a flag ([example](https://coderwall.com/p/kmchbw/zsh-display-commands-runtime-in-prompt))\r\n- **bash**: we achieve something similar to **zsh** using `$PROMPT_COMMAND` and DEBUG traps\r\n\r\nI think the timer module will be pretty light, just formatting and presenting the value passed in by the flag.\r\n\r\nDid you have another (perhaps simpler) solution in mind?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
