    "updated_at": "2019-07-26T05:15:06Z",
    "body": "Well that's a lot smarter than what I had in mind. I was thinking of computing the time within Rust, using `SystemTime` and `UNIX_EPOCH`. The problem there, of course, is that you have to interface the shell and starship twice per command--once for passing the initial time out into the shell so it can be stored, and a second for passing it back into starship on the prompt side.\r\n\r\nFor zsh, I think I'd prefer to append to the `preexec_functions` array, if it exists, so that we don't clobber the work any other frameworks are doing. I don't think such a mechanism exists for bash though.",
